---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SectionIntro from '../components/SectionIntro.astro';
import { profile } from '../data/profile';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="About James Moore, a Biochemistry Ph.D. student whose scientific interests span botany, biochemistry, chemical engineering, and computational biology."
>
  <div class="page-shell">
    <SectionIntro
      eyebrow="About"
      title="A scientist shaped by crossing boundaries."
      intro="My scientific interests have grown across plant biology, biochemistry, chemical engineering, and computational approaches to biological questions."
    />
    <div class="prose-grid">
      <div class="prose-main">
        <p class="lead-paragraph">
          I’m a {profile.role} at the {profile.institution}, working in the {profile.affiliation}.
          I expect to complete my doctoral studies in {profile.expectedGraduation}.
        </p>
        <p>
          My academic path has included undergraduate training in botany and biochemistry,
          master’s-level training in chemical engineering, and current doctoral study in
          biochemistry. Together, these perspectives shape how I approach biology: as
          experimental systems with molecular detail, quantitative structure, and practical
          constraints.
        </p>
        <p>
          I’m particularly interested in microbial natural products and synthetic biology.
          I value computational methods not as an end in themselves, but as a way to organize
          evidence, ask more precise questions, and make biological interpretation more transparent.
        </p>
        <p>
          Looking ahead, I’m interested in research scientist roles where experimental and
          computational perspectives can inform one another, including opportunities at
          national laboratories, academic research institutions, and biotechnology organizations.
        </p>
      </div>
      <aside class="fact-panel">
        <img
          class="about-portrait"
          src="/images/james-moore-headshot.jpg"
          alt="Portrait of James Moore wearing a lab coat"
          width="640"
          height="640"
          loading="lazy"
          decoding="async"
        />
        <p class="eyebrow">At a glance</p>
        <dl>
          <div><dt>Current role</dt><dd>{profile.role}</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Institution</dt><dd>{profile.institution}</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Research group</dt><dd>{profile.affiliation}</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Expected graduation</dt><dd>{profile.expectedGraduation}</dd></div>
        </dl>
        <p class="small-note">This is an independent personal portfolio and does not represent or imply institutional endorsement.</p>
      </aside>
    </div>
    <section class="principles" aria-labelledby="principles-heading">
      <div class="section-heading-row">
        <div><p class="eyebrow">Scientific approach</p><h2 id="principles-heading">What guides my work</h2></div>
      </div>
      <div class="principle-grid">
        <article><span class="principle-number">01</span><h3>Start with the biology</h3><p>Methods should serve the scientific question and the biological system being studied.</p></article>
        <article><span class="principle-number">02</span><h3>Keep evidence traceable</h3><p>Interpretation is stronger when sources, assumptions, and analytical steps remain visible.</p></article>
        <article><span class="principle-number">03</span><h3>Make work reproducible</h3><p>Clear records and repeatable workflows make it easier for others—and my future self—to follow the reasoning.</p></article>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
